# Day 05 — envs/prod/.gitignore

# State. Should never be here at all — this directory uses the S3 backend —
# but if `terraform init` is skipped, Terraform will happily write it locally.
# IAC-003 checks that no .tfstate file is committed.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Provider cache. Hundreds of MB per directory, machine-specific, regenerated
# by `terraform init`. This is the day's orphaned-disk-space trap.
.terraform/

# Saved plans can contain sensitive values in the clear.
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Real variable values.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: .terraform.lock.hcl
#
# The dependency lock file records exact provider versions and their
# checksums. Commit it — that is what makes `terraform init` reproducible for
# your colleagues and in CI. `terraform init -upgrade` is the only thing that
# should ever change it, and that change belongs in a reviewed PR.
# IAC-012 fires on any .gitignore that throws it away.
